WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.302
On this slide, we are focusing on catch a conversion error.

00:00:03.302 --> 00:00:08.052
Start with the meaning of the idea before worrying about the exact syntax.

00:00:08.052 --> 00:00:14.047
Ask what information is going in, what Python is doing with it, and what result should come out.

00:00:14.047 --> 00:00:19.102
A conversion error tells us the input does not satisfy our assumption.

00:00:19.102 --> 00:00:26.847
Real analytical workflows validate messy input instead of silently pretending it is correct.

00:00:26.847 --> 00:00:28.352
Before clicking Run, predict the output.

00:00:28.352 --> 00:00:34.497
Then run the cell, inspect the result, and change one value or condition at a time.

00:00:34.497 --> 00:00:37.842
Rerun it and explain why the output changed.

00:00:37.842 --> 00:00:42.856
The goal is to understand the relationship between input, process, and output.
